    //   = 13 bits → [W,W,B,B,W,W,W,B].
    // Row 1: 3 bits remain in buffer (lower 3 bits of byte 1 = 0b010 = VL1 code).
    //   VL1 fires (a0: 0→1, a0_color: true), then peek32 → avail=0 → break 421.
    //
    // Bit layout (16 bits = 2 bytes):
